  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-01-25T17:28:03.646Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I have been having high GPU Frametime spikes in random worlds since this patch dropped.  Worlds that used to run fine are now causing me to see spikes between 250-1000ms, crippling and crashing the client.  Some of these worlds are not even graphically-intense and sometimes the same world loads in fine hours later, and then fails again hours following.  It seems to have been worse on Saturday, but I am still experiencing problems with random worlds that I know I can run just fine.  This even occurs in private instances.  I also noticed that VRC seems to be using a lot more memory than normal, so maybe a possible leak?  Running an RTX 2060 paired with a Valve Index.",
